course: dictionary
lesson: 9307
title: Speckled: many small spots
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture for you. Speckled is one of them. When you see the word, picture a surface covered with lots of tiny spots of colour. «Young gulls are brown and speckled» means their feathers are brown with many small spots on them.
explain: Speckle can be a noun, a verb or an adjective. As a noun, a speckle is one small spot. As a verb, to speckle something means to cover it with spots. As an adjective, speckled describes something that already has spots, like a speckled egg.
explain: Look at the words around speckled to find its meaning. «Granite is a speckled igneous rock with big crystals» tells you the rock has many small marks of colour in it, not one big patch. The clue is in the word with: a sky speckled with stars is a sky dotted with stars.
fact: A speckle is a small spot or mark of colour.
fact: To speckle something means to cover it with lots of small spots.
fact: «Speckled» is an adjective that describes something covered in many small spots.
fact: Speckled eggs, trout and birds often blend into stones and leaves, which helps them hide.
fact: Artists speckle paint by flicking it off a toothbrush to make stars or sand.
exercise: «Young gulls are brown and speckled.» What does speckled mean here? | Bright blue all over | Cold and wet | Very fast and loud | *Covered with many small spots
exercise: Which words in «The speckled souslik has white dots» tell you what speckled means? | *white dots | squirrel | steppe | rare
exercise: Speckled eggs can blend into stones and leaves. What does blend into suggest? | *Look almost the same as the stones, so they are hard to see | Roll away down a hill | Shine brightly like glass | Make a loud crack
test: If you speckle a plate with paint, what do you do? | Wash it clean with water | *Cover it with lots of small spots | Break it into two pieces | Paint one big circle in the middle
test: Which word means covered with many small spots? | cloudy | *speckled | silent | smooth
exam: In «Young gulls are brown and speckled», what kind of word is speckled? | adverb | verb | *adjective | noun
